\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Histograms that show the distribution and median of calibration RMSE in the Monte-Carlo simulation that simulates $1000$ calibrations with semi-synthetic data. (Left:) Rotation error. The ground truth rotations have been sampled uniformly across $\text  {SO}(3)$. (Right:) Position error. The ground truth position vectors $\boldsymbol  {p} = [p_x, p_y, p_z]$ have been sampled uniformly across the interval $ p_x, p_y, p_z \in [-0.5, 0.5]$~m. Thus, the median position error corresponds to $\approx 3.0$~\% of the maximum sensor offset.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
